  Not necessarily in case 1.  

  You may have just found the wand and are trying to identify it.
(Wands of cancellation do not auto-identify under any
circumstances, as I currently misunderstand it.  ;-)

  A player doing this may not even know that cancellation exists,
much less what cancellation does.


  (Yes, there are better ways to try and identify a wand.  I'd
like to not restrict this to just knowledgable players. :-)


  In case 2, you know the monster is undergoing a cancellation
attempt because you identified the spell when you read it.
(And risked some negative effects in doing so, and at least
cost some time.)

  It's not really possible to cast an unidentified spell.  
(Wouldn't it be interesting if you could?  Read the spellbook
but the spell screen describes it as a "dusty" spell and
doesn't show the school, level, or failure probability.
The only way to find out what it does is to cast it.  If
the equivalent wand spell auto-identifies, so does the spell,
otherwise.... :-)

